 .707-.707l1.414 1.414a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .707M4.464 4.465a.5.5 0 0 1-.707 0L2.343 3.05a.5.5 0 1 1 .707-.707l1.414 1.414a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .708"></path></svg><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="18" height="18" fill="currentColor" class="bi bi-moon-fill theme-icon theme-icon--moon"><path d="M6 .278a.77.77 0 0 1 .08.858 7.2 7.2 0 0 0-.878 3.46c0 4.021 3.278 7.277 7.318 7.277q.792-.001 1.533-.16a.79.79 0 0 1 .81.316.73.73 0 0 1-.031.893A8.35 8.35 0 0 1 8.344 16C3.734 16 0 12.286 0 7.71 0 4.266 2.114 1.312 5.124.06A.75.75 0 0 1 6 .278"></path></svg></button></div><div class="d-flex align-items-center mt-4 mt-lg-0 me-lg-2"><a class="btn w-100" href="/api/site/auth/signin?state=%2F">Sign In</a></div><div class="d-flex align-items-center mt-4 mt-lg-0 "><a class="btn btn-dark btn-scale w-100" href="/pricing">Full Access →</a></div></div></div></div></nav><main class="flex-grow-1"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","@id":"https://cloudprice.net#breadcrumb","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://cloudprice.net","url":"https://cloudprice.net"}},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Azure VM Pricing","item":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://cloudprice.net","url":"https://cloudprice.net"}}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://cloudprice.net","url":"https://cloudprice.net","name":"Azure VM Sizes & Pricing Comparison","description":"Compare Azure Virtual Machine sizes, specifications, and pricing. Filter by VM series, vCPUs, memory, and storage.","dateModified":"09/23/2026 00:01:36","publisher":{"@id":"https://cloudprice.net/#organization"},"inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://cloudprice.net/#website"}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"CollectionPage","@id":"https://cloudprice.net#collection","name":"Azure Virtual Machine Catalog","description":"Comprehensive list of Azure VM sizes with on-demand, reserved, and spot pricing across all regions.","url":"https://cloudprice.net","dateModified":"09/23/2026 00:01:36","publisher":{"@id":"https://cloudprice.net/#organization"},"inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://cloudprice.net/#website"},"about":{"@type":"Thing","name":"1429 items available"}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://cloudprice.net#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","@id":"https://cloudprice.net#question-1","name":"How much do Azure VMs cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","@id":"https://cloudprice.net#answer-1","text":"Azure VM costs vary widely based on size, type, and region. The smallest burstable VMs start at just a few dollars per month, while high-performance computing and GPU instances can cost hundreds or thousands per month. You can save significantly with Azure Spot VMs (up to 90% savings) or reserved instances (up to 72% savings with 3-year commitments). Pricing varies by region, with some regions offering lower prices than others. Use CloudPrice to compare real-time pricing across all VM sizes and regions."}},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https://cloudprice.net#question-2","name":"What is the cheapest Azure VM?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","@id":"https://cloudprice.net#answer-2","text":"The cheapest Azure VMs are the smallest B-series (Burstable) instances like B1ls for Linux or B1s for Windows. These are ideal for development, testing, or low-traffic websites. The exact pricing varies by region, with some regions offering more competitive rates. For production workloads needing consistent performance, consider B2s or higher which offer better compute resources while remaining cost-effective. CloudPrice provides real-time comparison of the most affordable options across all Azure regions."}},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https://cloudprice.net#question-3","name":"What's the difference between Azure VM series?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","@id":"https://cloudprice.net#answer-3","text":"Azure VM series serve different workloads: B-series provides burstable performance for variable workloads and cost-sensitive applications, D-series offers balanced compute/memory for general-purpose applications, E-series delivers memory-optimized performance for databases and in-memory caching, F-series provides compute-optimized power for analytics and batch processing, N-series includes GPU acceleration for AI/ML and rendering workloads, and M-series offers massive memory capacity for SAP HANA and large enterprise databases. Choose based on your CPU, memory, storage, and I/O requirements."}},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https://cloudprice.net#question-4","name":"Are Azure spot VMs reliable?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","@id":"https://cloudprice.net#answer-4","text":"Azure Spot VMs offer deep discounts (up to 90% savings) but can be evicted with 30 seconds notice when Azure needs capacity. They're reliable for fault-tolerant workloads like batch processing, dev/test environments, stateless web servers, data analysis, and rendering jobs. Spot VMs are NOT suitable for databases, production web applications, or any workload requiring high availability and guaranteed uptime. Use Spot VMs with eviction policies and automatic restart configurations for best results."}},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https://cloudprice.net#question-5","name":"Azure vs AWS pricing: Which is cheaper?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","@id":"https://cloudprice.net#answer-5","text":"Azure and AWS have comparable pricing that varies by instance type, region, and workload. Neither is universally cheaper - the best value depends on your specific requirements. Azure often costs less for Windows workloads due to licensing benefits and hybrid use rights. AWS typically offers more granular instance sizing options. Both platforms offer significant savings with reserved instances (typically 40-70% off) and spot/preemptible pricing. Use CloudPrice to compare equivalent instances across both platforms for your specific configuration and region."}}]}</script><!--$--><!--$!--><template data-dgst="BAILOUT_TO_CLIENT_SIDE_RENDERING"></template><!--/$--><!--$!--><template data-dgst="BAILOUT_TO_CLIENT_SIDE_RENDERING"></template><!--/$--><!--$!--><template data-dgst="BAILOUT_TO_CLIENT_SIDE_RENDERING"></template><!--/$--><!--$!--><template data-dgst="BAILOUT_TO_CLIENT_SIDE_RENDERING"></template><!--/$--><!--/$--><div class="pt-3 container"><div><div class="azure-home-module-scss-module__JnaqYa__header"><div><h1>Azure VM Comparison</h1></div><div class="azure-home-module-scss-module__JnaqYa__sub_header"><div class="BatchExportBanner-module-scss-module__uSDaAG__banner"><a class="BatchExportBanner-module-scss-module__uSDaAG__bannerLink" href="/content/batch-export"><div class="BatchExportBanner-module-scss-module__uSDaAG__bannerContent"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" fill="currentColor" class="BatchExportBanner-module-scss-module__uSDaAG__icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M.5 9.9a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v2.5a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h12a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-2.5a.5.5 0 0 1 1 0v2.5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H2a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-2.5a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5z"></path><path d="M7.646 11.854a.5.5 0 0 0 .708 0l3-3a.5.5 0 0 0-.708-.708L8.5 10.293V1.5a.5.5 0 0 0-1 0v8.793L5.354 8.146a.5.5 0 1 0-.708.708l3 3z"></path></svg><div class="BatchExportBanner-module-scss-module__uSDaAG__text"><div class="BatchExportBanner-module-scss-module__uSDaAG__title">Batch Export API</div><div class="BatchExportBanner-module-scss-module__uSDaAG__subtitle">Download complete pricing datasets</div></div></div></a></div></div></div><br/><p>Discover and compare Azure Virtual Machines,<!-- --> <a href="/aws/ec2">Amazon EC2</a>, and<!-- --> <a href="/gcp/compute">GCP instance </a>specifications and pricing across multiple tiers, payment options, and geographical regions, all on one comprehensive page. Use the &#x27;Best Price Region&#x27; feature to quickly find where a specific VM offers the greatest value. For insights on optimizing cost vs. performance, visit our <a href="/performance">price/performance</a> analysis page.</p><p>The data is frequently updated from the Azure API, but may not be accurate. This site is not affiliated with Microsoft or Azure. The latest update occurred on<!-- --> <span style="background-color:var(--highlight-bg);padding:0 0.25rem">September 23, 2026 at 12:01 AM UTC</span></p></div><div class="data-grid-module-scss-module__e1jSJa__toolbar_selects"><div><div style="min-width:180px" aria-label="Currency"><div class="select__control select__control--placeholder"><div class="select__value-container"><span class="select__optionInner"><span class="select__label">US Dollar ($)</span></span></div><div class="select__indicators"><span class="select__dropdown-indicator" aria-hidden="true"><svg height="20" width="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M4.516 7.548c.436-.446 1.043-.481 1.576 0L10 11.295l3.908-3.747c.533-.481 1.141-.446 1.574 0 .436.445.408 1.197 0 1.615l-4.695 4.502c-.217.223-.502.335-.787.335s-.57-.112-.788-.335L4.516 9.163c-.408-.418-.436-1.17 0-1.615z"></path></svg></span></div></div></div></div><div><div style="min-width:180px" aria-label="Region"><div class="select__control select__control--placeholder"><div class="select__value-container"><span class="select__optionInner"><span class="select__label">East US (Virginia) / eastus</span></span></div><div class="select__indicators"><span class="select__dropdown-indicator" aria-hidden="true"><svg height="20" width="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M4.516 7.548c.436-.446 1.043-.481 1.576 0L10 11.295l3.908-3.747c.533-.481 1.141-.446 1.574 0 .436.445.408 1.197 0 1.615l-4.695 4.502c-.217.223-.502.335-.787.335s-.57-.112-.788-.335L4.516 9.163c-.408-.418-.436-1.17 0-1.615z"></path></svg></span></