served vm pricing,azure pricing calculator,azure vm cost,azure vs aws pricing,azure vm pricing east us,azure vm pricing west europe,azure cost optimization,best azure vm size,azure vm pricing comparison\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"4\",{\"name\":\"robots\",\"content\":\"index, follow\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"name\":\"googlebot\",\"content\":\"index, follow, max-video-preview:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"6\",{\"rel\":\"canonical\",\"href\":\"https://cloudprice.net\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"7\",{\"property\":\"og:title\",\"content\":\"Azure VM Pricing Comparison - 700+ Virtual Machine Sizes\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"property\":\"og:description\",\"content\":\"Find the most cost-effective Azure virtual machine for your workload. Compare all VM sizes with real-time spot, reserved, and pay-as-you-go pricing across all regions.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"9\",{\"property\":\"og:url\",\"content\":\"https://cloudprice.net\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"10\",{\"property\":\"og:image:alt\",\"content\":\"Azure VM pricing comparison on CloudPrice\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"11\",{\"property\":\"og:image:type\",\"content\":\"image/png\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"12\",{\"property\":\"og:image\",\"content\":\"https://cloudprice.net/opengraph-image-oo93ct?13bc75915ba3b0c2\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"13\",{\"property\":\"og:image:width\",\"content\":\"1200\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"14\",{\"property\":\"og:image:height\",\"content\":\"630\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"15\",{\"property\":\"og:type\",\"content\":\"website\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"16\",{\"name\":\"twitter:card\",\"content\":\"summary_large_image\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"17\",{\"name\":\"twitter:title\",\"content\":\"Azure VM Pricing - 700+ Sizes Compared\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"18\",{\"name\":\"twitter:description\",\"content\":\"Compare Azure VM pricing across all sizes and regions. Real-time spot, reserved, and pay-as-you-go pricing.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"19\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image:alt\",\"content\":\"Azure VM pricing comparison on CloudPrice\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"20\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image:type\",\"content\":\"image/png\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"21\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image\",\"content\":\"https://cloudprice.net/opengraph-image-oo93ct?13bc75915ba3b0c2\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"22\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image:width\",\"content\":\"1200\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"23\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image:height\",\"content\":\"630\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"24\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/favicon.ico?favicon.1f248965.ico\",\"sizes\":\"48x48\",\"type\":\"image/x-icon\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"25\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/favicon.ico\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"26\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/images/icons/favicon-16x16.png\",\"sizes\":\"16x16\",\"type\":\"image/png\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"27\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/images/icons/favicon-32x32.png\",\"sizes\":\"32x32\",\"type\":\"image/png\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"28\",{\"rel\":\"apple-touch-icon\",\"href\":\"/images/icons/apple-touch-icon.png\"}],[\"$\",\"$L19\",\"29\",{}]]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1a:Tea2,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"@id\":\"https://cloudprice.net#faq\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https://cloudprice.net#question-1\",\"name\":\"How much do Azure VMs cost?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"@id\":\"https://cloudprice.net#answer-1\",\"text\":\"Azure VM costs vary widely based on size, type, and region. The smallest burstable VMs start at just a few dollars per month, while high-performance computing and GPU instances can cost hundreds or thousands per month. You can save significantly with Azure Spot VMs (up to 90% savings) or reserved instances (up to 72% savings with 3-year commitments). Pricing varies by region, with some regions offering lower prices than others. Use CloudPrice to compare real-time pricing across all VM sizes and regions.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https://cloudprice.net#question-2\",\"name\":\"What is the cheapest Azure VM?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"@id\":\"https://cloudprice.net#answer-2\",\"text\":\"The cheapest Azure VMs are the smallest B-series (Burstable) instances like B1ls for Linux or B1s for Windows. These are ideal for development, testing, or low-traffic websites. The exact pricing varies by region, with some regions offering more competitive rates. For production workloads needing consistent performance, consider B2s or higher which offer better compute resources while remaining cost-effective. CloudPrice provides real-time comparison of the most affordable options across all Azure regions.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https://cloudprice.net#question-3\",\"name\":\"What's the difference between Azure VM series?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"@id\":\"https://cloudprice.net#answer-3\",\"text\":\"Azure VM series serve different workloads: B-series provides burstable performance for variable workloads and cost-sensitive applications, D-series offers balanced compute/memory for general-purpose applications, E-series delivers memory-optimized performance for databases and in-memory caching, F-series provides compute-optimized power for analytics and batch processing, N-series includes GPU acceleration for AI/ML and rendering workloads, and M-series offers massive memory capacity for SAP HANA and large enterprise databases. Choose based on your CPU, memory, storage, and I/O requirements.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https://cloudprice.net#question-4\",\"name\":\"Are Azure spot VMs reliable?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"@id\":\"https://cloudprice.net#answer-4\",\"text\":\"Azure Spot VMs offer deep discounts (up to 90% savings) but can be evicted with 30 seconds notice when Azure needs capacity. They're reliable for fault-tolerant workloads like batch processing, dev/test environments, stateless web servers, data analysis, and rendering jobs. Spot VMs are NOT suitable for databases, production web applications, or any workload requiring high availability and guaranteed uptime. Use Spot VMs with eviction policies and automatic restart configurations for best results.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https://cloudprice.net#question-5\",\"name\":\"Azure vs AWS pricing: Which is cheaper?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"@id\":\"https://cloudprice.net#answer-5\",\"text\":\"Azure and AWS have comparable pricing that varies by instance type, region, and workload. Neither is universally cheaper - the best value depends on your specific requirements. Azure often costs less for Windows workloads due to licensing benefits and hybrid use rights. AWS typically offers more granular instance sizing options. Both platforms offer significant savings with reserved instances (typically 40-70% off) and spot/preemptible pricing. Use CloudPrice to compare equivalent instances across both platforms for your specific configuration and region.\"}}]}"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8:[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"BreadcrumbList\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https://cloudprice.net#breadcrumb\\\",\\\"itemListElement\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":1,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Home\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"WebPage\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https://cloudprice.net\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://cloudprice.net\\\"}},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":2,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Azure VM Pricing\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"WebPage\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https://cloudprice.net\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://cloudprice.net\\\"}}]}\"}}],[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"WebPage\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https://cloudprice.net\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://cloudprice.net\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Azure V